Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:54:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] XU Mini M: platform for the MagicX XU Mini M; RK3326
 boards share a layer

Second SpruceMOSS-3326 board, so what the G350 had becomes a shared layer
(spruce's AnbernicXXCommon shape) and each board keeps only its own facts:

- SpruceMOSS3326Common.cfg / .sh: the SoC, twig-userspace and card values,
  and the device functions over Pixel2.sh. The RetroArch cfg path now
  follows $PLATFORM. G350.cfg sources it and adds its identity, joypad
  node, BTN_MODE menu key and SDL override; its exported environment is
  identical to before (121 variables, diffed). G350.sh and XUMiniM.sh are
  one-line includes.
- PyUI: SpruceMoss3326Device carries the constructor, key map and family
  names; BatlexpG350 and MagicxXuMiniM are constants.

XU Mini M (rk3326-magicx-xu-mini-m.dts over the XU10's):
- detection: rocknix,device_switch/this = xumini -> XUMiniM.
- pad: xu10-joypad (built in), "XU Mini M Gamepad" c3b0:0200. The Mini M's
  tree re-wires A/B/X/Y so the printed A sends BTN_EAST, as on the Pixel 2;
  menu is BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY1 (704), the Pixel 2's; no BTN_MODE. twig's
  gamecontrollerdb maps it by label already, so no SDL override. Raw order
  puts the d-pad at b12-b15 and menu at b16: flycast, yabasanshiro, the
  Saturn ES input and a mupen64plus section are the Pixel 2's translated by
  printed button onto that.
- panel: portrait 480x640 with rotation = <90>. sway turns the UI from
  fbcon/rotate; the initramfs draws /flash/logo.bmp raw, so the shared
  device_init turns the image's landscape logo once for a board that sets
  PANEL_LOGO_ROTATION, and the Boot Logo app writes it turned 90.
- per-platform copies of the Pixel 2's defaults, first-boot flag, USB
  storage (strings from BRAND/PLATFORM), backup list.

Unrun on hardware; the kernel and its dtb (this = "xumini") build.
